msgstr ""
"**?localId** - :ref:`scalar <Records_API_scalar>` from :ref:`Records API "
"<Records_API>`, which returns the local part of the global entity "
"reference. For example, for **emodel/person@someuser** the local part is "
"**\"someuser\"**"

#: ../../settings_kb/processes/ecos_bpmn/editor/components/ecos_bpmn_components_script_task.rst:448
msgid "Загрузка идентификаторов из ассоциаций"
msgstr "Loading identifiers from associations"

#: ../../settings_kb/processes/ecos_bpmn/editor/components/ecos_bpmn_components_script_task.rst:450
msgid ""
"При работе с ассоциациями в скриптах важно учитывать разницу между "
"``.id`` и ``?id``:"
msgstr ""
"When working with associations in scripts, it is important to consider "
"the difference between ``.id`` and ``?id``:"

#: ../../settings_kb/processes/ecos_bpmn/editor/components/ecos_bpmn_components_script_task.rst:452
msgid ""
"``.id`` — возвращает часть ссылки после ``@`` (localId). Например: "
"``emodel/authority-group@accountant`` → ``accountant``"
msgstr ""
"``.id`` — returns the part of the reference after ``@`` (localId). For "
"example: ``emodel/authority-group@accountant`` → ``accountant``"

#: ../../settings_kb/processes/ecos_bpmn/editor/components/ecos_bpmn_components_script_task.rst:453
msgid ""
"``?id`` — возвращает полную ссылку. Например: ``emodel/authority-"
"group@accountant``"
msgstr ""
"``?id`` — returns the full reference. For example: ``emodel/authority-"
"group@accountant``"

#: ../../settings_kb/processes/ecos_bpmn/editor/components/ecos_bpmn_components_script_task.rst:455
msgid "Для передачи значений в другие ассоциации используйте ``?id``:"
msgstr "To pass values to other associations, use ``?id``:"

